- [ ] Consolidated 2.0.0 release notes <!-- id: k1 labels: docs blockedBy: k16, k2 -->
      Every 1.x since 1.28.0 is a 2.0 beta. Write the single 2.0.0 section from the 1.x changelog entries; it is what Sparkle and the download page will show.

- [ ] Document the new features on the Cockpit page of the site <!-- id: k2 labels: docs -->
      `../site`: .env.cockpit, Restart tab, Neovim, workspace CLI, remote hosts, Gallery documents, Database panel and everything else that shipped since the page was last updated.

- [ ] Multi-window: detach a terminal tab <!-- id: k15 labels: feature -->
      Needs the PTY hosted outside the window process. The sidecar terminal gateway (remote mode) already does that: make it the default local path, then detaching becomes attaching the same session id in another window. Bonus: terminals survive a UI crash. Decide whether this lands in 2.0 or after.
      <!-- comment: 2026-09-17T12:00 -->
      Decided: not in 2.0. Blocker k10 is done; the real cost is elsewhere. "Open in new window" today is a document window that only receives the file path and boots no Cockpit module, so it works for markdown/.kanban/.notebook (state lives in the file) but not for tabs whose state lives in the main app: .dbq (connections, Keychain secrets, DB isolate, SSH tunnels, access guardrails), Mongo/Redis browsers, HTTP, task output, and terminals (PTY is a child of the window). Detaching needs the main app or a sidecar to own the state and windows to become thin clients (the CLI socket already runs DB queries). Open when resumed: scope (any tab vs terminal only, .dbq as its own card), state owner (main app vs sidecar), move the live session vs reopen.

