- [x] Agent profiles: run Claude Code / Codex with different accounts (sandboxed or per-profile config) <!-- id: k24 labels: decision -->
      Need a way to launch a harness (Claude Code, Codex CLI, Pi) under a different account or isolated config per workspace or per tab, e.g. a personal and a work account side by side. Open question: build it in Cockpit (per-profile HOME / CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR / CODEX_HOME injected into the terminal env, like .env.cockpit does) or delegate to an existing tool (containers, devcontainers, `sandbox-exec`, direnv, a profile manager). Investigate what each harness supports natively (Claude Code honours CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR; Codex uses CODEX_HOME) before deciding. Park until the 2.0 core items are done.
      <!-- comment: 2026-09-15T16:00 -->
      Decision: no new feature. Claude Code has no built-in profile flag; the only native mechanisms are `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` (whole account: credentials, settings, history) and `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` (credential only); Codex uses `CODEX_HOME`. `.env.cockpit` already injects these per workspace (they are not in the blocklist), so the flow is: add `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/abs/path/.claude-work` to the workspace `.env.cockpit`, restart the tabs, run `claude` and `/login` once. Orca does the same thing internally and still has an open issue for multiple subscriptions. Follow-ups: document the recipe on the site (k2) and, if wanted later, a per-account usage/rate-limit indicator like Orca's status bar.

